    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="0916" n="904" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.248/6–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-11T10:00:00+03:06">June 11, 1945—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>235. Re Dept’s 156, June 5.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d887-f1"/> King Abdul Aziz has
                    telegraphed that he agrees to postponement of my visit to Riyadh as he wishes
                        <pb facs="0917" n="905" xml:id="pg905"/> negotiations to be comprehensive
                    including all proposals of US Govt in Saudi Arabia. He expects to hear from me
                    before the end of June officially on the matters broached to him tentatively in
                    Dept’s 131, May 7.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d887-f1" n="24" xml:id="d887-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 1151, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
